  "goodToKnow": "Der Sportwagen is a sports car: Porsche (based in Stuttgart, the 911 built since 1963/64), Mercedes-AMG and BMW M are famous German makes. Germany's motorways are known for sections without a general speed limit, though a recommended 130 km/h applies. Confusingly, der Sportwagen is also a pushchair for toddlers who sit up, unlike der Kinderwagen (pram). Plural: die Sportwagen (southern: Sportwägen)."
